{"backendEventChannel":"assistant","backendEventContent":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, Write<\/tools-used-before-summary>\n<\/system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Riela workflow `table-count-guideline-review` (session 3); I am the **author** node. Write in Japanese `docs\/table-count-guideline.md`: how to get a whole-table row count of huge MySQL tables as fast as possible without degrading the service or locking, for any table design. Rules (verbatim constraints):\n   - \"Never connect to any database other than the local compose lab.\" Scripts connect only to lab hosts `primary`, `replica` (or the fresh matrix server passed by argv) and must restore anything they change. \"Do not edit the shared table data.\" \"Do not commit or push.\" \"Do not spawn agents or invoke other workflows.\" \"You have no shell, on purpose.\" \"You cannot use web search.\" Mark unconfirmed docs as unconfirmed.\n   - To measure: write `bench\/requested\/<experiment-id>.py` (optional `.versions`; supported 8.4.0, 8.4.13, 9.7.0, 9.7.4, 26.10.0); the next step (lab-runner) runs every new\/edited script (20 min limit each; step limit 4 h), then I'm called to integrate results.\n   - Every number names its results file; separate measured\/documented\/reasoning; keep doc concise, remove superseded text; keep `bench\/countlib.py` and `bench\/count_preflight.py` consistent with the guideline. Treat reviewQuestions as input. Respond to EVERY finding by stable ID: `fixed` (sections+evidence), `disputed` (counterevidence), `unresolved` (blocker). Reviewers decide closure.\n   - \"Run verification and shell commands in the foreground. Do not launch detached\/background commands.\"\n   - **Output of this step**: return raw JSON only (no fences\/prose): `{\"when\":{\"always\":true},\"payload\":{...}}` with `workflowInput` (preserved), `revision` (now **11**), `guidelinePath`, `guidelineSha256` (read back & hash), `authorResponses`, `experimentsWritten`, `discussionHistory`, `unresolvedQuestions` (also preserve findings\/requestedExperiments, by reference is what I've done). \"In this step write the experiments and any guideline changes that do not depend on them.\"\n\n   workflowInput (preserve exactly):\n   {\"acceptanceCriteria\":[\"Opus 5.5 と GPT-6.1 Sol の両方の敵対的レビューを経て、high\/middle の未解決指摘がない\",\"数値はすべて results\/ のファイルに基づき、未計測は明記されている\",\"ガイドライン本文のSQLがラボで実行され、結果が確認されている\",\"テーブル設計ごとに推奨方法と根拠がある\",\"データ・インデックスによるロック要因と、その事前検知方法がある\"],\"constraints\":[\"対象はMySQLのサポート中バージョン(8.4 LTS, 9.7 LTS, 26.10 Innovation)のみ\",\"接続先はローカルのcomposeの検証環境のみ\",\"コミットとpushはしない\",\"人間が読む文書は日本語\"],\"guidelinePath\":\"docs\/table-count-guideline.md\",\"requestedWork\":\"複数の巨大データサービスを運用する開発者向けに、MySQLテーブルの全件カウント(業務上のWHEREなし)を、サービス性能を落とさず全件ロックせず最速で取得する方法のガイドラインを、計測結果に基づいて日本語で作成する。良い方法を洗い出し、あらゆるデータベース\/テーブル設計で成り立つことを敵対的に検証する。\"}\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   Split count (form A\/B cursors, hint MAX_EXECUTION_TIME), Max_execution_time_exceeded counter classification, PENDING MDL check, long-success rule, job ceiling (rows+seconds), roundtrip_advance; CountMonitor; replica stop\/count\/restore with single channel gate; rpl_stop_replica_timeout (STOP failure stays in force, error 1875); secondary-index MVCC clustered lookups under scattered writes; buffer pool eviction; open-loop Workload; Sampler; lab.rb runs new\/edited scripts in byte-sorted name order and status-file mtime rule; matrix server: `--memory 1500m --cpus 2`, BP 256M, db `bench` must be created, `connect(host, db=\"mysql\")` first; Python 3.9 in bench container (no same-quote nesting in f-strings); `query(c, sql, None)` does no % formatting. `builder()` connection has sql_log_bin=0 (use for private schema DDL so replica isn't broken); replica filter is `replicate-do-table=bench.t_repl`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `bench\/countlib.py` — EDITED this turn:\n     * `restore_applier(host, stop_failed=False, deadline_seconds=30.0, poll=.25, settle=.5)`: returns `{stop_failed, starts_issued, saw_stopped, restored, unresolved_stop, last_state, seconds}`; after a failed STOP returns restored=True only after seeing No and starting; at deadline restored=False, unresolved_stop=True.\n     * `replica_point_count(replica, table, max_execution_ms=60_000, kill_hook=None, stop_failure_grace=60)`: uses `restore_applier(replica.host, stop_failed=stop_failed, deadline_seconds=stop_failure_grace if stop_failed else 30.0)`; status gets `:applier_not_confirmed` suffix if not restored.\n     * `split_count(..., long_success_factor=2, max_rows=None)`: `if max_rows and total >= max_rows: return finish(\"stopped:max_rows\")` before max_steps check. Other args: `c, table, plan, width, limit_ms, duty, pause_ms, stop, partition, check_roundtrip, enforce_plan, min_width, max_steps, on_step(n,ms,cursor), before_statement, cursor_codec, keep_sql, db, expected_limit_ms, max_seconds, check_advance, pending_check`.\n     * Others available: `session_setup(c, ms)`, `split_plans`, `forced_plan(c, db, table, index)`, `split_statements`, `plan_check`, `CountMonitor(host, db, table, job_id, stop, interval, connect_fn, recheck_instrument, max_hll)`, `replica_channels(c)`, `enum_split_count`, `key_args`.\n   - `bench\/reqmix.py` — EDITED this turn: `_arm(b, kind, plan=None, index=None, ceiling=\"rows\")`: split uses `limits = {\"max_rows\": ROWS*3}` (or max_steps when ceiling != \"rows\"), records `step_log`, `slowest_steps_at_s_and_ms`, and `step_ms_by_10s` (the dict comprehension I wrote is clumsy\/O(n²)-ish; simplify to a loop). `write_mix2_body(script_id, mix, total_rate)` (lines 114–190, shown above) NOT yet edited. MIXES: `indexed`, `uniform_insert_delete`, `monotonic_insert_delete`. ROWS=20M, SPLIT_SECONDS=150, STATEMENT_LIMIT_MS=120000. `pkonly_body` also there.\n   - `bench\/reqlib.py`: `guard(id, est_min)` (budget 215 min from marker), `Results(id, answers, **meta)` with `.section(name)`, `.time_left()` (1140 s), `.save()`, `.finish()`; `sql_try`, `builder(host, db)`, `reset_schema`, `global_status(c,*names)`, `session_status(c, pattern)`, `measured_run(label, wl, method, base, recover, during, table, host, sampler_host, replica_host, data_locks, watcher)`, `bounded(seconds, fn,...)`, `cpu_ticks`, `equal_windows`.\n   - `bench\/lablib.py`: `connect(host, read_timeout, cursor, autocommit, db=\"bench\")`, `query`, `Workload(table, key, max_id, write_col, head, readers, writers, rate, host, write_sql, read_sql)` with `.start\/.finish\/.window(t0,t1)\/.samples`, `Sampler(table, host, replica_host, data_locks)` with `.start\/.finish\/.window\/.rows`, `pin`, `METHOD_CPU`.\n   - `bench\/requested\/02-EXP-S8-REPLICA-STOP-FAILURE.py`: template for STOP-failure tests (`block_applier`, row id 50,000,001 in t_repl, `SET GLOBAL rpl_stop_replica_timeout=2`, restore in finally, delete ids>=50000000, `ALTER TABLE t_repl AUTO_INCREMENT=20000001`). Don't edit it (kw `stop_failure_grace` retained).\n   - `bench\/requested\/00-budget-start.py`: must be rewritten (edit print text to \"round 4 (revision 11)\") to reset clock.\n   - `bench\/requested\/3a-EXP-O6-LOOP-RULES.py`: to edit for max_rows arms.\n   - Scripts NOT mine, read, lab-only, unedited: `90-wide-count-forms.py`, `91-encrypted-count.py` (edited 09:42 by someone; `.encrypted`, `.versions`), `92-wide-form-order.py` (bench_wide2, evicts with t_dense), `93-metadata-accuracy.py` (ANALYZE on all shared tables, SET GLOBAL innodb_stats_persistent_sample_pages, req_uneven schema), `94-metadata-on-replica.py` (inserts 2M 'bulk' rows into t_repl then deletes, STOP\/START replica, toggles super_read_only, lab_reader user, probe94 column). 92-wide\/93\/94 have no status so will run next lab round, unguarded, after mine (~50 min worst). 90\/91 have status (no rerun unless edited). `lab.rb` has `.encrypted` support added by someone else; results `requested_wide_count_forms.json`, `requested_encrypted_count_{8.4.13,9.7.4,26.10.0}.json`, `results\/requested\/manual-91.txt`, `manual-run.txt` exist from a run outside the workflow.\n   - `bench\/requested\/README.md`: needs order paragraph + mapping updates.\n   - `docs\/table-count-guideline.md`: no edits yet this turn. Relevant lines: 12 (conclusion table row), 21, 75–76 (flow note on FORCE PRIMARY), 278 (rule 4 ceiling), 361, 363, 737, 1076, 1077 (`90-wide-count-forms.json` citations), 387, 389, 392 (write-shape table\/bold), 395, 810 (延長の条件), 834 (STOP paragraph), 1062 (§10), 1100–1102 (§11), §8 停止条件 at ~916.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Bash is restricted: heredocs with braces, `${}`, `mv`, `shasum`, `git log`, python syntax check, some grep with `\\|` get \"requires approval\"\/rejected. Don't work around; use Read\/Edit\/Write; simple `ls`, some `grep`, `tail` work. guidelineSha256 has been reported as UNAVAILABLE each round with an honest note (reviewers compute it).\n   - Can't rename\/delete files; reorder by creating new names and stubbing old ones.\n   - Past script bugs: e_dec 1062, MD5 1305 on 9.7\/26.10 (use LPAD\/SHA2), single shared connection lost arms in 3e\/3f; all fixed in earlier rounds.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Latest review (revision 10, rejected). Open findings to answer:\n   - FIND-O10-PRIMARY-SCALE (middle): FORCE PRIMARY recommendation over-generalised from 2 GB table (1.3× pool) at 800\/s; at 100\/s no established difference vs k. Fix: short-limit comparison trials in flow\/§1\/§7, mark unmeasured combos; run EXP-O10-PRIMARY-SCALE.\n   - FIND-O10-INDEXED-100-STALL (middle): requested_05 drift_arm stopped:max_steps at 66.806 s; whole_run_write p95 1646.57, p99 2345.55, max 2764.58 ms; comparison arms' write p99 max 466.43. Add to text as unexplained; include service tail tolerance in stop decisions; run EXP-O10-INDEXED-100-STALL.\n   - FIND-S8-REPLICA-STOP-FAILURE-01 (middle, reopened): old restore claimed restored 