r ROW-CEILING), `tail=False` (for STALL: after normal arms run split_pk ≥5 times alternating with no-count control of same length, 1 Hz log thread of Innodb_buffer_pool_pages_dirty, pages_flushed, os_log_written, data_fsyncs, HLL, disk reads; save windows for every tail arm), save write\/read\/server windows for drift arm too.\n   b. New scripts (byte order sorts first; each with `guard`, IDs equal to filenames):\n      - `00-budget-start.py` rewrite.\n      - `0c`–`0g` EXP-O10-PRIMARY-SCALE via new `bench\/reqscale.py` `scale_body(script_id, host, version?, mix, share, rows)`: `.versions`=8.4.13 (256 MB pool); argv host version; build `bench.seq` then `bench.t (id BIGINT PK AUTO_INCREMENT, k BIGINT NOT NULL, v INT NOT NULL, pad CHAR(60) DEFAULT 'x')` with sql_log_bin=0, ADD KEY k_k(k) after load (CRC32 k), ANALYZE; closed-loop capacity probe 15 s (8 threads, host-specific) then rate=10% or 30%; mixes indexed (UPDATE k=k+1; split k skipped as moving) and uniform INSERT+DELETE; own connection per arm, rotating order, ≥3 repeats: statement k and statement PRIMARY hint 300000, split k\/PK (width 10000, 500 ms, max_rows=rows*3, max_seconds=150), control of equal length; after 1 hit of 300 s skip further; record seconds, Handler deltas, pool read requests, disk reads, write p50\/p95, write in 10 s before arm (backlog), HLL, miss after (window t1..t1+10), time_left guard. Scripts: `0c` indexed-10pct, `0d` indexed-30pct, `0e` uniform-10pct, `0f` uniform-30pct (10M rows), `0g` uniform-10pct 20M rows (8×).\n      - `0h-EXP-O10-ROW-CEILING-indexed-800`, `0i-EXP-O10-ROW-CEILING-uniform-800` (split_only, new IDs so 06\/08 results are retained).\n      - `0j-EXP-O10-INDEXED-100-STALL` (write_mix2_body indexed 100 with tail).\n      - `0k-EXP-O10-NOPK-FORCE`: private t_nopk design (a,b,KEY k_a; writes INSERT + `DELETE ... WHERE a=%s LIMIT 1`, max_id 1000) and t_uniq_notnull design (code UNIQUE NOT NULL, v, KEY k_v(v); UPDATE v WHERE code) 5M rows; forms: FORCE INDEX(PRIMARY) (exp